from rest_framework.views import APIView
from rest_framework.response import Response
from rest_framework import permissions, status
from django.contrib.sites.shortcuts import get_current_site
from .models import CustomerOrder
from .serializers import CustomerOrderSerializer

class OrderDetailView(APIView):
    permission_classes = [permissions.IsAuthenticated]

    def get(self, request, order_id):
        current_site = get_current_site(request)
        try:
            # Enforce object scoping to both customer and current site
            order = CustomerOrder.objects.get(id=order_id, customer=request.user, site=current_site)
        except CustomerOrder.DoesNotExist:
            return Response({'detail': 'Order not found on this storefront'}, status=status.HTTP_404_NOT_FOUND)

        serializer = CustomerOrderSerializer(order)
        return Response(serializer.data)
